Test Case: other_hibernation
================================================================================

Initial Error:
Error: Attempt to get attribute from null value

  on azapi.tf line 56, in resource "azapi_resource" "this":
  56:       type         = identity.value.type
    ├────────────────
    │ identity.value is null

This value is null, so it does not have any attributes.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: The dynamic identity block uses can() to check if module.replicator.azapi_header.identity exists, but can() returns true even when the value is null. Then accessing identity.value.type fails because the value is null.
- Fix Method: Change the for_each condition to properly check for null values using != null instead of can()
- Changes Made: Change line 54 from:
    for_each = can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity) ? [module.replicator.azapi_header.identity] : []
  To:
    for_each = module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null ? [module.replicator.azapi_header.identity] : []
- Result: Success. Terraform plan now succeeds and shows acceptable drift only (ignore_null_property, locks, output, replace_triggers_external_values, sensitive_body_version, type, timeouts).

Final Result: Fix successful

